    "details": "<p><strong>Introduction:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>On the occasion of Engineer&rsquo;s Day (15th September 2026), the Entrepreneurship Cell of Meerut Institute of Technology is organizing Navachar - Code Fest 2026, a competitive coding fest hosted on Unstop.</li>\n<li>The objective of this event is to provide students with a platform to showcase their problem-solving skills, enhance their logical thinking, and compete with the best coding talent in the college.</li>\n<li>Whether you are a beginner or an advanced programmer, Navachar will help you learn, compete, and grow.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Event Name: Navachar &ndash; Code Fest 2026</li>\n<li>Organized By: E-CELL MIT MEERUT</li>\n<li>Date: 15th September 2026</li>\n<li>Mode: Online (via Unstop Platform)</li>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to all college students</li>\n<li>Registration Fee: Free</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Certificates:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Winner Certificate &ndash; Awarded to one winner from each year-based round</li>\n<li>Participation Certificate &ndash; Provided to all participants</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Format and Rounds:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Round 1 &mdash; MCQ Challenge\n<ul>\n<li>Date &amp; Time: 15th September 2026</li>\n<li>Duration: 30 minutes</li>\n<li>Format: 30 Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)</li>\n<li>Topics Covered: Programming basics, logical reasoning, aptitude, and general problem-solving</li>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to all participants</li>\n<li>Shortlisting Criteria:\n<ul>\n<li>1st Year students will end their participation here</li>\n<li>2nd, 3rd, and 4th Year students qualifying here will move to Round 2</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Round 2 &mdash; Medium-Level Coding Challenge\n<ul>\n<li>Date &amp; Time: 15th September 2026</li>\n<li>Duration: 60 minutes</li>\n<li>Format: Three coding problems</li>\n<li>Topics Covered: Data structures, algorithms, and implementation-based coding</li>\n<li>Eligibility: Only for 2nd, 3rd, and 4th Year students</li>\n<li>Shortlisting Criteria:\n<ul>\n<li>2nd Year students will end their participation here</li>\n<li>3rd and 4th Year students qualifying here will move to Round 3</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Round 3 &mdash; Hard-Level Coding Challenge\n<ul>\n<li>Date &amp; Time: 15th September 2026</li>\n<li>Duration: 90 minutes</li>\n<li>Format: Two advanced coding problems</li>\n<li>Topics Covered: Optimized algorithms, dynamic programming, and problem-solving under constraints</li>\n<li>Eligibility: Only for 3rd and 4th Year students</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Only college students are allowed to participate</li>\n<li>Registration using the official college email ID is mandatory</li>\n<li>Participants must select their correct year of study while registering</li>\n<li>Participants are only allowed to attempt rounds applicable to their year</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each participant must register individually through Unstop</li>\n<li>Multiple registrations from the same participant are strictly prohibited</li>\n<li>Use of AI tools, ChatGPT, GitHub Copilot, or plagiarism is not allowed</li>\n<li>Stable internet connectivity is mandatory during the event</li>\n<li>Any unfair means will lead to immediate disqualification</li>\n<li>The decision of the organizing committee will be final and binding</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MCQ Round: Based on the number of correct answers and completion time</li>\n<li>Coding Rounds:\n<ul>\n<li>Code correctness and accuracy</li>\n<li>Time complexity and optimization</li>\n<li>Number of successful test cases passed</li>\n<li>In case of a tie, preference will be given to the participant with the earliest correct submission</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>FAQs:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Q1. Who can participate?<br />Any college students can register.</li>\n<li>Q2. Is there any registration fee?<br />No, participation is free.</li>\n<li>Q3. How will certificates be distributed?<br />Certificates will be generated automatically via Unstop.</li>\n<li>Q4. What if I face technical issues during the event?<br />A dedicated support team will be available. Contact details will be shared after registration.</li>\n</ul>",
